# Manual QA Assessment: Bug Evidence

Bug evidence from a manual QA technical assessment I completed for a previous job application. The app under test was a Spanish-language inventory web app with a login, user management and a product stock screen.

I captured each issue as an annotated screenshot or a short screen recording. Red marks show where the problem appears.

## Evidence

| File | What it shows |
| --- | --- |
| [BUG01.gif](evidence/BUG01.gif) | Screen recording on the login page: username filled in, password empty, then "Entrar" is clicked. The username field is empty after the page reloads. |
| [BUG02.PNG](evidence/BUG02.PNG) | Users list with a user whose last name is blank (marked in red). |
| [BUG03.PNG](evidence/BUG03.PNG) | "Registrar usuario" form with the "Crear" button marked in red. |
| [BUG04.PNG](evidence/BUG04.PNG) | Users list where special characters in a last name display incorrectly (marked in red). |
| [BUG05.PNG](evidence/BUG05.PNG) | Users page with the left navigation menu marked in red. |
| [BUG06.PNG](evidence/BUG06.PNG) | Stock page ("Productos en existencia") with the page header area marked in red. |
| [BUG07.gif](evidence/BUG07.gif) | Screen recording of the stock page: product search for "girl", then the Excel export opened in a spreadsheet. |
| [BUG08.PNG](evidence/BUG08.PNG) | A stock quantity shown as `[object Object]` instead of a number (marked in red). |
| [Typo_1.PNG](evidence/Typo_1.PNG) | Spelling mistake in the "Registrar usuario" form (underlined in red). |
| [Typo_2.PNG](evidence/Typo_2.PNG) | Spelling mistake in the page title "Productos en exsitencia" (underlined in red). |

## What this shows about my approach

- Functional testing of login, user creation and stock screens.
- Checking input handling with special characters and blank fields.
- Visual and text checks (typos and display errors).
- Clear evidence: one issue per capture, annotated, with screen recordings for steps that need motion.
